cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite the thesis below."
title: PlazDraughts
abstract: >-
  An AlphaZero-style self-play engine for Italian draughts: a PyTorch residual
  policy-value network and Monte Carlo Tree Search, with a C++20 engine for
  batched multi-threaded self-play and LibTorch inference, orchestrated in a
  repeated SELF-PLAY -> TRAIN -> ARENA cycle and measured against fixed-depth
  opponents, frozen generations and an external engine. Implementation studied
  in a Bachelor's thesis on end-to-end deep reinforcement learning for chess and
  Italian draughts.
type: software
